# Source: Ventrax AV4 report. Acceptance specification; execution is verified separately.
Feature: Initial purchases, subscriptions and technical billing

  Scenario: Confirm an initial purchase
    Given an initial purchase order exists and payment has not been verified
    When Billing receives and validates a successful payment confirmation
    Then Billing records the verified purchase and makes the confirmation available for account provisioning

  Scenario: Reject an invalid payment confirmation
    Given a purchase order exists
    When an invalid or unverifiable payment confirmation is received
    Then Billing does not mark the purchase as paid

  Scenario: Prevent duplicate payment processing
    Given a payment transaction has already been recorded
    When the same provider confirmation is received again
    Then Billing does not create a duplicate transaction or repeat the resulting business action

  Scenario: Store only tokenized payment information
    Given the principal user authorizes a payment method through Niubiz
    When Billing records the payment method
    Then Billing stores only the permitted token and masked card information
    And Billing does not store PAN or CVV

  Scenario: Activate Pro after verified payment
    Given the principal user has Free and requests Pro
    When Billing verifies the subscription payment
    Then Billing activates Pro and records its paid validity period

  Scenario: Preserve Pro until the paid period ends
    Given a user has an active paid Pro period
    When a recurring payment attempt fails
    Then Billing preserves the current Pro benefits until the paid period ends
    And Billing does not extend the subscription without verified payment

  Scenario: Apply full Pro coverage at visit completion
    Given a technical visit has been completed
    And the principal user's Pro subscription was active at the completion timestamp
    When Billing evaluates the technical service coverage
    Then Billing records full coverage for the applicable service cost

  Scenario: Charge a Free technical visit after completion
    Given a technical visit has been completed
    And no applicable Pro coverage exists at its completion timestamp
    When Billing determines the pending technical charge
    Then Billing creates the corresponding payable amount without duplicating previous charges

  Scenario: Restrict financial operations to the principal user
    Given an authenticated subuser has delegated meter permissions
    When the subuser attempts to manage cards, payments or subscriptions
    Then Billing denies the operation

  Scenario: Register the result of electronic invoicing
    Given a transaction requires an electronic tax document
    When the corresponding document is generated and processed
    Then Billing records its identifier, status and applicable tax authority response
